<title>UK: EU sold 44,750 T sugar at 45.512 Ecu rebate.</title>
<headline>EU sold 44,750 T sugar at 45.512 Ecu rebate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total 44,750 tonnes of current series white sugar received export rebates of a maximum 45.512 European Currency Units (Ecus) per 100 kilos at Wednesday's European Union (EU) tender, the U.K. Intervention Board said.</p>
<p>Out of this, traders in France received 27,250 tonnes, in Germany 11,500 and in Belgium and the UK 3,000 tonnes each, it added.</p>
</text>
